  ("How much does a Kepler heat pump cost installed in Ontario?", "A Kepler heat pump installed by EHI starts at $5,500, and most central systems in the 2 to 3 ton range come in below comparable premium brands once ductwork and electrical work are included. Your quote is guaranteed before any work starts, and a qualifying model can return up to $7,500 through the Home Renovation Savings Program."),
  ("Does a Kepler heat pump work at -30°C?", "Yes. Kepler cold-climate heat pumps are rated to keep heating at -30°C, which covers nearly every winter night across Ontario. For Northern Ontario homes or anyone who wants extra backup, we pair it with a gas furnace or an electric air handler with auxiliary heat."),
  ("Is a Kepler heat pump eligible for the Ontario heat pump rebate?", "A Kepler heat pump is eligible when the exact model and size are on NRCan's qualified products list, which we check before quoting. Pre-approval must be in place before installation, so we file it first and confirm your eligibility. Program terms can change."),
  ("How quiet is a Kepler heat pump?", "Kepler heat pumps are quiet enough that most homeowners stop noticing them after the first week, because the inverter compressor runs at low speed for most of the day. We also place the unit away from bedroom windows and on anti-vibration mounts."),
